<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry VI the Good</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1294">1294</a>–<a href="/years/1335">1335</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Henry VI of Wrocław</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry VI the Good was a Piast duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wroclaw">Wrocław</a> in Silesia from 1311. Pressed by his relatives, who took much of his inheritance, and caught between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, he recognised the overlordship of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">King John</a> of Bohemia in 1327, with Wrocław to pass to Bohemia on his death. He died without sons in 1335.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-vi-the-good.jpg" alt="Henry VI the Good" width="320" height="428" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anton Boys · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Henryk_Dobry.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
